# Donna, run locally (README.md, "Run Donna locally").
# Copy to .env and fill in. `npm run local:runtime`, `npm run local:web`,
# `npm run demo:fi:load`, `npm run demo:fi:record` and `docker compose up`
# read this file. The zero-key demo (`npm run demo:fi`, or the compose `demo`
# service) needs none of it and reads no key from it. A line starting with #
# is off; remove the # to set it. Never commit .env.

# ── Required ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The key you type on the sign-in screen. The runtime refuses firm data
# without it. Any long random string, e.g. from `openssl rand -hex 24`.
DONNA_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# ── Model providers (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without keys Donna starts, shows the demo company and stores uploads, but
# reads no document. With a key, the contents of documents and of the books
# are sent to that provider. At start the runtime prints which lanes are lit.

# OpenAI: document routing and extraction, bank-statement reading, coding,
# ask drafting.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Anthropic: receipt and invoice extraction (unified extractor),
# reconciliation triage, bank-line disposition, merchant lookup, chat.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Typesafe (api.typesafe.ai), optional: with both values set it makes the
# first-line decisions for matching, bank and document disposition and coding.
# Without them that lane is dark and OpenAI and Anthropic make those decisions.
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
# TYPESAFE_MODEL=
# Override the model id for every OpenAI / Anthropic call. Leave unset to use
# each task's own default model.
# OPENAI_MODEL=
# LOUIS_MODEL=
# Shadow challenger (any OpenAI-compatible endpoint). Records evidence only;
# runs only when all four are set.
# OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_BASE_URL=
# OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_MODEL=
# MODEL_CHALLENGER_CAP_TOKENS=

# ── Local runtime (optional; each comment gives the default) ──────────────

# Where the database, uploaded documents, backups and logs live.
# Default: ~/.donna-desktop
# DONNA_DESKTOP_DATA_DIR=
# Port of the runtime API on 127.0.0.1. Default: 8787
# DONNA_DESKTOP_PORT=
# Port of the web app on 127.0.0.1. Default: 5173
# DONNA_LOCAL_WEB_PORT=
# Address the web app listens on. Default: 127.0.0.1 (this machine only).
# DONNA_LOCAL_WEB_HOST=
# With `docker compose up`, docker-compose.yml fixes the data paths, the
# database, PG_BIN, DONNA_DESKTOP_PORT and DONNA_LOCAL_WEB_HOST inside its
# containers (the web app is published on the host's 127.0.0.1 only);
# everything else here is read.
# Postgres 16 bin directory (holds pg_ctl and initdb). Default: looked up in
# the usual install paths (/usr/lib/postgresql/16/bin, Homebrew, Postgres.app).
# PG_BIN=
# Suffix of the private Postgres socket; change only to run two books at
# once. Default: 5433
# DONNA_DESKTOP_PG_PORT=
# Uploaded documents. Default: <data dir>/documents
# DONNA_DESKTOP_BLOB_DIR=
# Backup packages. Default: <data dir>/backups
# DONNA_DESKTOP_BACKUP_DIR=
# When the daily backup runs (a cron expression) and how many to keep.
# Default: 30 1 * * * and 14
# DONNA_DESKTOP_BACKUP_CRON=
# DONNA_DESKTOP_BACKUP_KEEP=
# Set to off to run the API without background jobs (diagnostics only).
# DONNA_DESKTOP_SCHEDULER=
# Kill switch: a comma-separated list of capability flags to force off, or
# `all`. It can only switch a capability off, never on. Example:
# JEV_RECONCILIATION stops the first-line lane even where Typesafe is set.
# CLIENT_CONFIG_FORCE_DISABLE=
